| `tests/integration/test_frontend_lockfile_gate.py` | Fails a frontend app the Makefile's `FE_APPS` glob names whose `package-lock.json` git does not track, whose lockfile predates the root package entry, or whose root entry records other dependencies than its `package.json`, and a configured `layers.frontend.stack` git tracks no app for, so CI's npm installs the tree the author tested. | `make test` | [`layers.frontend.stack`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Reads what git tracks: in a tree outside any git repository it skips, and with no app and no stack it skips naming the project as having no frontend. It compares the manifest with the lockfile's root entry, not with the resolved tree below it. Not the install itself: `make fe-install` runs npm. | [deterministic-checks.md](../guides/deterministic-checks.md) | always |
